          deepDive: "**V-るべくしてV-た** repeats (usually) the same verb: 起こるべくして起こった, 売れるべくして売れた. べく is a form of the classical auxiliary べし (the source of べき, *should / be bound to*), so the phrase says *~ happened as it was bound to happen*. The book: 状況からわかるように、当然の結果として〜になった — given the circumstances, **the result was inevitable**, not luck or coincidence.\n\nIt works in both directions:\n- **Bad outcomes** (criticism): 指摘された欠陥を放置していたのだから、これは起こるべくして起こった事故だ (*they left the defect alone after it was pointed out, so this accident was waiting to happen*). This is how the detective uses it.\n- **Good outcomes** (deserved success): この車は燃費も良く、洗練されたデザインで、売れるべくして売れたと言える (*with its fuel economy and refined design, it was bound to sell well*); 彼女は選ばれるべくして選ばれた (*she was chosen because she deserved it*).\n- **Destiny**: 私たち2人はめぐり会うべくしてめぐり会った (*we were meant to meet*).\n\nConnection (book): **V₁-る + べくして + V₂-た**; for する, **すべくして** also occurs (成功すべくして成功した); V₁ and V₂ are usually the same verb. It is typically followed by と言える / と言えよう / のだ / と言わざるを得ない, which gives it an evaluative, written tone (the formal icon).\n\nConstraint: the context must supply a **reason** that makes the outcome inevitable, usually stated right before or after: 考え方が違っていたから、別れるべくして別れた (*their ideas were different, so they were bound to split up*); 原作が大人気のマンガで声優も一流…ヒットするべくしてヒットした. A chance reason contradicts it: ✗たまたま運が良かったから、選ばれるべくして選ばれた.\n\nCompare the べし family in this book:\n- **Vべく** (#90): *in order to ~* (formal purpose): 優勝すべく練習を重ねた (*practiced hard in order to win*).\n- **〜べくもない** (#122): *there's no way ~*: 知るべくもない (*there was no way of knowing*).\n- **〜べからず** (#111): prohibition, *must not*: 芝生に入るべからず (*keep off the grass*).\n- **〜べきだ** (N3): *should* — an obligation, not an inevitability.\n\nCommon mistake: reading it as *should have happened* (obligation). べくして…た reports that something **did** happen, just as it naturally would.\n\nJLPT tip: pick the reason that makes the outcome unavoidable (ずさんな経営体質, not 健全な). Check: 今日の試合は負けるべくして負けたと思います。自分たちの力を過信していたのが敗因です (*we were bound to lose — we were overconfident*); the review passage: 能力からいって、一番優秀な僕が選ばれるべくして選ばれたんだ.",
